Mutation run for test_golden_fixtures.py (P1-16), 2026-10-23.
Method: a scratch copy of packages/, scripts/ and pyproject.toml; one mutation per run (a corrupted or
removed fixture, a mutated generator, a mutated coverage script, or a dropped model rule in the copy of
src); then the whole of test_golden_fixtures.py (681 tests) is run in the copy. KILLED = at least one
test fails. The repository itself was never edited. The harness is mutation-harness.py.txt.

Run 1 (63 mutants, code before the last two test additions): 61 killed, 2 survived.
Survivors of run 1: C04, C05.
  C04 (the coverage script ignores boolean values) survived because no test removed a fixture that
      holds the only value of a boolean; fixed by adding two boolean points to
      test_property_coverage_script_reports_gaps_and_exits_non_zero.
  C05 (an over-broad exclusion in the coverage script) survived because the exclusion test checked the
      reasons, not the excluded set; fixed by asserting the exact number of excluded points per entity
      in test_property_coverage_exclusions_are_the_unreachable_points_and_nothing_else.
Run 2 (final code): the baseline stays green and C04, C05 and F20 are killed (below).

